# HooshyarOS Cline / Kilo execution rules

## Role
Cline and Kilo Code are local VS Code execution/operator layers. They are NOT the architecture owner and must not redefine Architecture Freeze V4, governance, product semantics, or completion rules.

## Source of truth
Always read, in order:
1. Docs/HOOSHYAROS_MASTER_CHARTER.md
2. Docs/HOOSHYAROS_GOVERNANCE_CHARTER.md
3. Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
4. Docs/COMMERCIAL_PRODUCT_COMPLETION_CONTRACT.md
5. Assistant/SYSTEM_PROMPT.md
6. Docs/Product/PRODUCT_CONSTRUCTION_ROADMAP.json
7. Docs/Product/PRODUCT_PLATFORM_MANIFEST.json
8. Docs/Product/PRODUCT_QUALIFICATION_MATRIX.json

The Manifest defines what the product is. The Qualification Matrix defines what must be proven. Never replace either with intuition.

## Autonomous lifecycle law
The Assistant/construction fabric is the lifecycle owner for routine mechanical construction, repair, standardization, commercialization, qualification, evidence production and continuation. Cline and Kilo are execution/operator layers, not manual workflow coordinators and not architecture owners.

The canonical lifecycle is:
`READ -> AUDIT -> DISCOVER -> PRIORITIZE -> PLAN -> DEPENDENCY CHECK -> CHECKPOINT -> IMPLEMENT -> FOCUSED TEST -> INTEGRATE -> RUNTIME/APPLICATION ACCEPTANCE -> VERIFY -> REPAIR IF NEEDED -> STANDARDIZE -> COMMERCIALIZE -> QUALIFY -> EVIDENCE -> COMMIT/PUSH -> CI FEEDBACK -> REPLAN`

Human shell commands may bootstrap or explicitly approve governed actions, but Cline/Kilo must not require the human to manually stitch routine lifecycle stages together. When the current stage produces a factory/CI/acceptance failure, the operator must transition into the canonical repair path rather than repeatedly retrying the failed command unchanged.

## Canonical reuse law
Before creating or proposing any new Agent, Engine, Tool, Service, orchestration layer, business semantic or provider-specific construction path, inspect the existing canonical architecture, Engine/Capability registries, Assistant/Builder/Planner/Orchestrator components, autonomous runtime and repair runners, Product runtime/services, tests, evidence collectors and CI/release workflows.

Prefer reuse and composition of existing canonical components. Duplicate agents, duplicate engines, parallel orchestration hierarchies, duplicated business rules and external coding-agent dependencies are prohibited unless an explicit governing architecture decision proves a genuine missing capability or contradiction.

## Mandatory execution loop
Run the real product factory, not a simulated audit:
`READ -> AUDIT -> SELECT -> IMPLEMENT -> TEST -> INTEGRATE -> RUN -> ACCEPT -> REPAIR -> TEST -> ACCEPT -> COMMIT -> PUSH -> REPLAN`

Use `npm run product:cline:audit` as the first full-platform review command, then `npm run product:factory` as the primary local acceptance command.

## Full-platform review
For a product-affecting task, run `npm run product:cline:audit` before changing code. Review the complete surface: architecture, capabilities, engine ownership, APIs, UI/dashboard, persistence, security, Windows/Web/Android runtime, tests, CI workflows, packaging, release scripts, and deployment contracts. The audit writes `.hooshyar/cline-platform-audit.json` and maps every required Qualification Matrix cell to static status. Static review never upgrades a runtime/acceptance/CI cell to PASS.

## Approved local execution operators
Kilo Code is an approved local VS Code execution/operator layer alongside Cline. It may inspect the repository, execute governed commands, apply the smallest implementation repair, run verification, produce evidence, and perform Git operations when safely automatable.

Kilo Code must obey the same source-of-truth order, lifecycle, scope discipline, evidence protocol, security boundaries, Git discipline and anti-drift rules defined here and in the Governance Charter.

Kilo Code does not have authority to redefine Architecture Freeze V4, governance decisions, product semantics, completion rules, or canonical engine/capability ownership.

Provider choice for the operator is an implementation detail. No external coding provider, model, SaaS service or agent may become a hidden architectural dependency or mandatory HooshyarOS runtime component.

## Repair behavior
When the factory returns BLOCKED or the governed verification path fails:
- automatically enter the canonical repair path;
- first obtain or generate the canonical `ASSISTANT_REPAIR_MISSION` from the failure evidence;
- the human must not be required to manually invoke a repair handoff during routine autonomous execution;
- identify the first failing stage, Matrix cell, environment, workflow, and root cause;
- inspect and reuse the existing governed repair capability/runners before introducing anything new;
- make the smallest coherent repair;
- never weaken/remove a failing test to obtain green;
- never modify Architecture Freeze V4 to bypass a failure;
- add or update a regression test for the repaired defect;
- rerun `npm run product:cline:audit`;
- rerun focused verification;
- rerun `npm run product:factory`;
- after application acceptance passes, run `npm test -- --runInBand`;
- preserve failure and repair evidence and re-plan automatically after verification.

Repeated blind retries of an unchanged failing command are prohibited. If a persistent failure is not safely repairable within the governed budget, enter BLOCKED with evidence instead of looping indefinitely.

## Agent repair evidence
A completed repair is not trusted until `.hooshyar/agent-repair-success.json` exists and `npm run product:agent:evidence` passes. The evidence must be type `ASSISTANT_REPAIR_MISSION_V1_RESULT`, status `PASS`, and bound to the current commit. It must identify the mission/finding, list an actual implementation change, report regression status `PASS`, and report factory acceptance status `PASS`. Never fabricate this file and never mark `ci-feedback` PASS without it.

## Product acceptance
A green engine/unit test is not commercial completion. The real Windows journey must pass:
`health -> ready -> session -> tenant -> ingestion -> financial analysis -> dashboard -> restart -> same tenant -> restored dashboard`.

Equivalent customer workflows must be proven for Web and Android before those environments are marked PASS.

## Evidence protocol
Every finding must contain:
- severity
- evidence source
- Manifest layer
- Qualification Matrix cell
- environment
- workflow
- root cause
- required change
- regression verification
- acceptance verification
- release impact

Unknown is not PASS. BLOCKED is not PASS. Passing one environment never proves another environment.

## Git discipline
Before risky changes create a checkpoint/commit when possible. Keep one coherent capability/fix per commit. Do not force-push. Do not push or merge unless the repository policy explicitly permits it.

## Operator boundary
Cline and Kilo may execute commands, inspect the repository and available GitHub evidence, apply the smallest governed repair, and run verification. Neither is permitted to invent a new engine, duplicate business semantics, alter Architecture Freeze V4, or claim product completion without application and acceptance evidence.
